# The image's own entries for the programs that accept connections (LISTENERS in /etc/amethystora/security.conf):
# what the image's own services listen on, which starts when the watcher may already have looked, recorded and
# not said. The machine's own are in /etc/amethystora/allow.d/listeners (ame security allow listeners "PROGRAM
# PORT"). A glob each.
#
# fwupd's passim, which offers the firmware metadata fwupd downloaded to the machines nearby; it starts when
# firmware is looked for, from Updates or GNOME Firmware (P2pPolicy in /etc/fwupd/fwupd.conf)
passimd 27500
# The phone link (amethystora-connect, whose name the kernel cuts to fifteen characters), for phones, from the first
# login, which may come after the watcher's first run: the protocol's port 1716, and one port of 1739 to 1764 for a file
# in transit. The firewall opens them at home only (ame security home-networks)
amethystora-con 1716
amethystora-con 173[9]
amethystora-con 174[0-9]
amethystora-con 175[0-9]
amethystora-con 176[0-4]
